# Federal Tax Administration Proclamation No. 983/2016 — የፌዴራል ታክስ አስተዳደር አዋጅ ቁጥር 983/2008

Federal Negarit Gazette Extraordinary Issue, 22nd Year No. 103, Addis Ababa, 20 August 2016. The English text as published by the Ministry of Revenue on mor.gov.et (an English-only PDF; the Ministry lists the law as in force). The Ministry's copy does not say whether later amendments are consolidated into it, so where a figure matters, check it against the Gazette.

**Amended and renumbered in 2026.** The Tax Administration Proclamation (Amendment) No. 1434/2026 (30 July 2026, in force on publication) added conciliation of tax disputes as new Articles 61–71 and renumbered the old Articles 61 to 139 as Articles 72 to 156: old 61–85 became 72–96 (+11) and, after six more new articles on revising assessments (97–102), old 86–139 became 103–156 (+17). The article numbers below are the numbers in this 2016 text, with the new number in brackets where it changed. 1434/2026 also rewrote the failure-to-issue-invoice penalty, the notice of appeal article, the amended-assessment time limits and the rules on new evidence; see its own file in this library.

## What this law covers (in brief)

The procedure for every federal tax: registration and the TIN, record keeping, receipts and sales register machines, filing declarations, assessments, payment, collection and enforcement, refunds, objections and appeals, tax clearance, rulings, the Tax Appeal Commission, tax agents, administrative penalties and tax offences.

## Key articles

- Art. 9 — a person who becomes liable for tax must apply for registration in the approved form, with proof of identity including a biometric identifier, within 21 days of becoming liable. An employer applies for the registration of a new employee who is not yet registered.
- Art. 10 — a registered person notifies changes (name, physical or postal address, constitution, principal activity, banking details, electronic address) in writing within 30 days.
- Art. 11 — a person who no longer needs to be registered for any tax applies for cancellation in the approved form within 30 days; the Authority cancels by written notice within 30 days of the application and may carry out a final audit within 90 days of that notice. It may also cancel on its own motion (for example when the person has died or a company has been liquidated).
- Art. 13 and 15 — one TIN for all tax laws, and only one at a time; the TIN is cancelled when the registration is cancelled, when it was issued under a false identity, or when the person already had a TIN.
- Art. 19 — a taxpayer who must keep books registers the type and quantity of receipts with the Authority before printing them, and must issue a receipt for every transaction.
- Art. 20 — the use of sales register machines (cash register and point-of-sale machines) is governed by a Council of Ministers regulation.
- Art. 21 — declarations are filed in the approved form; a body's declaration is signed by its tax representative or licensed tax agent.
- Art. 32 — a taxpayer may apply in writing for more time to pay or to pay by instalments; late payment interest still runs from the original due date.
- Art. 37 — late payment interest: the highest commercial lending rate of the previous quarter increased by 15%, simple interest computed daily.
- Art. 54 — objection to a tax decision: in writing within 21 days of service of the decision, stating the grounds, after paying the part of the assessment that is not disputed.
- Art. 56 — appeal to the Tax Appeal Commission is valid only after paying 50% of the tax in dispute (penalty and interest not counted). Art. 88 [now 105] — the notice of appeal is filed within 30 days of service of the decision.
- Art. 57 — appeal from the Commission to the Federal High Court within 30 days, on a question of law only, after paying 75% of the tax in dispute.
- Art. 61 [now 72] — tax clearance certificate: issued within 14 days if the taxpayer has met its tax obligations; no government body issues or renews a licence or admits a taxpayer to a public tender without one. 1434/2026 added a conditional clearance for taxpayers with a pending objection or appeal or an instalment agreement.
- Art. 101 [now 118] — failure to register: 25% of the tax payable for the period of non-registration, or Birr 1,000 per month when that is more; failure to apply for cancellation: Birr 1,000 per month.
- Art. 104 [now 121] — late filing: 5% of the unpaid tax for each period, up to 25%; at most Birr 50,000 for the first period; not less than the lower of Birr 10,000 or 100% of the tax; Birr 10,000 per period when no tax was due.
- Art. 105 [now 122] — late payment: 5% of the tax unpaid one month after the due date plus 2% for each further month, never more than the tax.
- Art. 106 [now 123] — failure to withhold or to pay over withheld tax: 10% of the tax; the responsible officers of a body Birr 2,000 each (sub-article 2 as rewritten by 1434/2026).
- Art. 108 [now 125] — failure to issue a tax invoice: this text says Birr 50,000 per transaction; 1434/2026 replaced it with Birr 100,000 for each invoice not issued, which may not be waived.
- Art. 109 — understatement: 10% of the shortfall, 30% the second time, 40% after that.
- Art. 113 [now 130] — sales register machines: Birr 50,000 for unaccredited machines or software, or for selling without a machine receipt (except while the machine is under repair); Birr 100,000 for tampering with the fiscal memory; Birr 25,000 for obstructing inspection or missing the annual inspection, and for having no service contract, not connecting to the terminal or not keeping the inspection booklet; Birr 10,000 for not reporting theft or irreparable damage within three days, or a malfunction within four hours.
- Art. 117 [now 134] — obtaining more than one TIN, lending one's TIN or using another's: fine of Birr 20,000 and one to three years' simple imprisonment.
- Art. 120 [now 137] — trading without issuing a tax invoice: fine of Birr 25,000–50,000 and three to five years' rigorous imprisonment; under 1434/2026 criminal liability for not issuing an invoice arises only after two administrative penalties for the same act in one tax period.
- Art. 125 [now 142] — tax evasion (concealing income, or not filing or paying with intent to evade): fine of Birr 100,000–200,000 and three to five years' rigorous imprisonment.

## በአማርኛ በአጭሩ — ይህ ሕግ ምን ይሸፍናል

የፌዴራል ታክስ አስተዳደር አዋጅ ቁጥር 983/2008 የሁሉም የፌዴራል ታክሶች አሠራርን ይደነግጋል፦ ምዝገባና የግብር ከፋይ መለያ ቁጥር (TIN)፣ የሂሳብ መዝገብ፣ ደረሰኝና የሽያጭ መመዝገቢያ መሣሪያ፣ ማሳወቂያ፣ የግብር ውሳኔ፣ ክፍያና ማስፈጸሚያ፣ ቅሬታና ይግባኝ፣ የታክስ ክሊራንስ፣ አስተዳደራዊ ቅጣቶችና የወንጀል ድንጋጌዎች። ሙሉ ጽሑፉ ከታች በእንግሊዝኛ ነው። በ2018 ዓ.ም. የወጣው ማሻሻያ አዋጅ ቁጥር 1434/2018 የማስማማት (conciliation) ድንጋጌዎችን እንደ አዲስ አንቀጽ 61–71 በማከሉ ቀድሞ ከአንቀጽ 61 እስከ 85 የነበሩት ወደ 72–96፣ ከ86 እስከ 139 የነበሩት ደግሞ ወደ 103–156 ተሸጋግረዋል። ይህ ማጠቃለያ የሕጉ ኦፊሴላዊ ትርጉም አይደለም።

## ዋና ዋና ድንጋጌዎች

- አንቀጽ 9 — ግብር የመክፈል ግዴታ ያለበት ሰው ግዴታው ከተጀመረ በ21 ቀናት ውስጥ በጸደቀው ቅጽ፣ ማንነቱን በሚያሳይ ማስረጃ (ባዮሜትሪክን ጨምሮ) መመዝገብ አለበት።
- አንቀጽ 10 — የስም፣ የአድራሻ፣ የዋና ሥራ ወይም የባንክ መረጃ ለውጥ በ30 ቀናት ውስጥ በጽሁፍ ይገለጻል።
- አንቀጽ 11 — ከሁሉም ታክሶች ምዝገባ የማያስፈልገው ሰው በ30 ቀናት ውስጥ ምዝገባው እንዲሰረዝ ያመለክታል፤ ባለሥልጣኑ በ30 ቀናት ውስጥ ይሰርዛል፣ በ90 ቀናት ውስጥ የመጨረሻ ኦዲት ሊያደርግ ይችላል። (የTIN መመለሻ ቅጽ፦ https://bina.et/tax-forms)
- አንቀጽ 19 — የሂሳብ መዝገብ የሚይዝ ግብር ከፋይ ደረሰኝ ከማሳተሙ በፊት ማስመዝገብና ለእያንዳንዱ ግብይት ደረሰኝ መስጠት አለበት።
- አንቀጽ 32 — የክፍያ ጊዜ ማራዘሚያ ወይም በክፍያ መክፈል በጽሁፍ ሊጠየቅ ይችላል፤ የዘገየ ክፍያ ወለድ ግን ከመጀመሪያው ቀን ይታሰባል።
- አንቀጽ 54 — በግብር ውሳኔ ላይ ቅሬታ ውሳኔው ከደረሰ በ21 ቀናት ውስጥ በጽሁፍ፣ ምክንያቱን ገልጾና ያልተከራከረበትን ግብር ከፍሎ ይቀርባል።
- አንቀጽ 56 እና 88 [አሁን 105] — ለግብር ይግባኝ ኮሚሽን ይግባኝ በ30 ቀናት ውስጥ፣ የተከራከረበትን ግብር 50% በመክፈል (ቅጣትና ወለድ ሳይጨምር)።
- አንቀጽ 57 — ከኮሚሽኑ ወደ ፌዴራል ከፍተኛ ፍርድ ቤት በ30 ቀናት ውስጥ፣ በሕግ ጥያቄ ብቻ፣ የተከራከረበትን ግብር 75% በመክፈል።
- አንቀጽ 61 [አሁን 72] — የታክስ ክሊራንስ ግዴታውን ለተወጣ ግብር ከፋይ በ14 ቀናት ውስጥ ይሰጣል፤ ያለ ክሊራንስ ፈቃድ አይሰጥም አይታደስም፣ በመንግሥት ጨረታ መሳተፍ አይቻልም። 1434/2018 ቅሬታ ወይም ይግባኝ ላለው ወይም በክፍያ ስምምነት ላይ ላለ ግብር ከፋይ ሁኔታዊ ክሊራንስ አክሏል።
- አንቀጽ 101 [አሁን 118] — ያለመመዝገብ፦ ላልተመዘገበበት ጊዜ ከሚከፈለው ግብር 25% ወይም በወር 1,000 ብር (ከፍተኛው)፤ ምዝገባ እንዲሰረዝ ያለማመልከት፦ በወር 1,000 ብር።
- አንቀጽ 104 [አሁን 121] — ማሳወቂያ ማዘግየት፦ ካልተከፈለው ግብር ለእያንዳንዱ ጊዜ 5% እስከ 25%፤ ለመጀመሪያው ጊዜ ከ50,000 ብር አይበልጥም፤ የሚከፈል ግብር ከሌለ ለእያንዳንዱ ጊዜ 10,000 ብር።
- አንቀጽ 105 [አሁን 122] — ክፍያ ማዘግየት፦ ከአንድ ወር በኋላ 5%፣ ከዚያ ለእያንዳንዱ ወር ተጨማሪ 2%፤ ከግብሩ መጠን አይበልጥም።
- አንቀጽ 108 [አሁን 125] — የታክስ ደረሰኝ ያለመስጠት፦ በዚህ ጽሑፍ በአንድ ግብይት 50,000 ብር፤ በ1434/2018 ላልተሰጠ ለእያንዳንዱ ደረሰኝ 100,000 ብር ሆኗል፣ አይነሳም።
- አንቀጽ 113 [አሁን 130] — የሽያጭ መመዝገቢያ መሣሪያ፦ ያለ መሣሪያው ደረሰኝ መሸጥ 50,000 ብር፤ ፊስካል ሜሞሪ ማበላሸት 100,000 ብር፤ ዓመታዊ ምርመራ ያለማድረግ 25,000 ብር፤ ብልሽትን በ4 ሰዓት፣ ስርቆትን በ3 ቀናት ውስጥ ያለማሳወቅ 10,000 ብር።
- አንቀጽ 125 [አሁን 142] — ግብር ለመሰወር ገቢ መደበቅ ወይም ያለማሳወቅ፦ ከ100,000 እስከ 200,000 ብር መቀጮና ከ3 እስከ 5 ዓመት ጽኑ እስራት።
